  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Higher Education Reform in Science and Engineering in Togo, PARESI phase 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Support to Higher Education Reform in Science and Engineering (PARESI) Phase 2 project in Togo aims to support higher education reform in science and engineering by building and equipping research and teaching laboratories of international standards in Lom&#xe9;, Kara, and Atakpame, strengthening partnerships, and providing scholarships.  
Specifically, the project addresses the challenges and needs of the public universities of Lom&#xe9; and Kara as well as the &#x201c;Ecole Normale&#x201d; of Atakpame, such as the lack of fully functional academic laboratory, equipment, human resources, and quality assurance in the fields of science and engineering. The project will benefit students, lecturers, researchers, and the economy of Togo by enhancing the capacity, quality, relevance, and innovation of higher education in science and engineering. PARESI phase 2 will also adopt a participatory, gender-responsive, climate-resilient, and conflict-sensitive approach to ensure its sustainability and impact. Finally, a particular attention will be given to the rolling out the ICT/Digital technology approach promoted by the government of Togo, including, setting up a comprehensive real-time monitoring and evaluation system with the use of mobile phone and open-source software technology throughout the project implementation, and through the IsD</narrative>
  </description>
